WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.233
Two of

00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:00.800
the world's most

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.003
powerful diplomats sat face to face

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.637
earlier on Thursday.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:05.872
US Secretary of State

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.273
Antony Blinken and Russia's

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:08.308
Foreign Minister

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:09.576
Sergei Lavrov

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:10.710
met on the sidelines

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.946
of the G20 meeting in New Delhi.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:14.080
A US official

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.949
says Blinken underscored U.S.

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:17.183
support for Ukraine

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.918
during the roughly ten minute

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.054
meeting in prepared remarks earlier,

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:21.654
Blinken said

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.123
the unprovoked invasion

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:24.424
had marred the G20

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:26.326
meeting of foreign ministers.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.093
He called it

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.229
an attack on the core principles

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:31.831
of the United Nations charter.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:32.565
Since Carney

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.234
Atwood joins us

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.969
from the US State Department

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:36.770
in Washington.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.671
I can't even speak to your sources

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:39.305
about

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:40.206
what was discussed

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.442
in that remarkable 10 minutes.

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:43.143
Yeah, that's right.

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:45.211
So this was a meeting on the sidelines

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:46.346
of the G20

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.847
foreign ministers meeting in India.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:48.782
As you said,

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.784
and there were essentially three things

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:52.519
that the Secretary of state addressed

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:54.554
with the Russian foreign minister.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:55.355
First

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:56.823
was urging Russia

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:59.225
to come back into compliance

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.093
with New Start.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:00.493
Of course,

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.227
that's a single

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:02.262
lasting arms

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:04.464
control treaty between the US and Russia

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.399
that Russia suspended

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:07.901
just earlier this year.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.369
Second, he urged Russia

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:11.571
to release an American

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.440
who is wrongfully detained in Russia.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.641
That's Paul Whalen.

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.509
And third, as you were saying

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:19.345
earlier there, he also reiterate did U.S.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:20.880
support for Ukraine.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.482
This is the first time

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:24.350
that these two men,

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.952
the top diplomats from the U.S.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.921
and Russia, have met face to face

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.289
and had a conversation

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:30.623
Since before Russia's

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.958
invasion into Ukraine.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:35.161
They last met in early 20, 22.

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:36.162
At that time,

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.130
the secretary of state

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:40.166
warned Lavrov about the consequences

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.103
that would occur if they did invade

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:43.803
Ukraine.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:45.572
Obviously, they went ahead with that.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.806
And we do know that

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:48.241
they had one conversation,

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.309
at least

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:50.910
over the course of the last year,

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.679
not in person, but by telephone.

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:53.880
That was this summer

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.682
when they were discussing negotiations

00:01:55.682 --> 00:01:56.483
to release

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:57.183
Brittney Griner,

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.084
who was American

00:01:58.084 --> 00:01:59.519
wrongfully detained in Russia

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:00.687
at the time.

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.222
But it's also significant, Max,

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:03.289
that they have actually been

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:04.124
in the same place

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:05.391
at the same time

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.793
over a number of times

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.761
over the course of the last year.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:09.796
You know, in Bali

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.564
for another foreign ministers

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:13.233
meeting at the United Nations,

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.501
they've been in the same room.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:15.702
They haven't had discussions.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.637
So the fact that the secretary of state

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:19.772
approached the Russian foreign minister,

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.241
according to a senior State

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.008
Department official,

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:23.176
is pretty significant

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:24.511
because he clearly felt

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:25.445
that there were messages

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:28.848
that he wanted to portray in person Okay.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:30.483
Thank you very much indeed,

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.318
working your sources on that.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.053
Ukraine's military says

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:35.722
it's still holding its ground

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.023
in the city of banknotes,

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.491
but admits it's getting

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.093
increasingly difficult.

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:41.027
Ukrainian officials

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:41.628
report heavy

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:43.496
fighting on the outskirts of the city

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.097
and they suggest

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:45.732
Russian forces have advance

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.600
within the city itself

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.403
about 4500 civilians remain in the city.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.538
As Russian troops

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:52.172
to close

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.339
in Ukraine

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.073
also reports

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.109
a series of Russian rocket attacks

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:57.777
on a multi-story apartment building

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:59.646
in the city of submarines here.

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.981
The attack killed at least three people.

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:03.416
Emergency crews

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.451
managed to rescue nine people, including

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:06.853
a pregnant woman

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:09.389
about five kilometers from park.

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:12.592
But as the town of Joseph HCR,

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:14.127
many Ukrainians fled there

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:16.429
to escape the fierce battles in modes.

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:18.097
However, the military fears,

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:21.634
if bad falls to CVR, will be next.

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:25.071
Alex Marquardt is there

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:28.041
This is the road

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.742
on the way to back mud

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:32.045
cars, military vehicles

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:34.681
bombing up and down this road, going to

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.417
and from the front.

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:41.254
You see this armored vehicle right here

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:45.024
the sign for victory.

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:47.193
There are still some people here,

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:48.027
not too many,

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.263
but some of these hardy residents

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:51.164
have stayed behind

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:53.466
This is the Shop of Sea views.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:54.567
Who is here?

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.536
Grilling meats held shashlik.

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:58.738
He actually fled from back mount

00:03:58.738 --> 00:03:59.973
two months ago

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:01.507
and has opened up the shop

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:04.310
selling basics like bananas, beetroot and

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.745
and candles.

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:06.813
There's another man who here

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:07.480
who we just met

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.949
whose daughter is still in back mud.

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:12.285
One of the thousands of people there

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:15.021
who have been asked to evacuate

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.589
but are still in the city.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.391
Amid this incredible fighting,

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:19.225
you can see that

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:20.994
they put up wood there

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:22.729
too, to protect those windows.

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:25.832
So much destruction in this town.

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:27.734
We were just farther in

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.002
the center of town, is called it,

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:29.669
because if you are,

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:32.272
this is one town over from back

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.107
with a large group of people

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.041
